mission file: ./SMission/dive240_xanthos.mi ...
 ============================================================

 dive240_xanthos.mi

 240-second dive to 15 m using the controller settings logged

 by Xanthos during the September 1998 Massachusetts Bay LOOPS

 cruise (X9827208.obd).



 Differences from dive240.mi:

   - Outer-loop depth-mapping gain dropped 6x (0.5 -> 0.08).

     This is the dominant change; the original simulator value

     drove the controller into pitch-limit saturation.

   - Pitch loop kpp/kdp/kip raised to match real-vehicle gains.

   - Heading loop kih added (small integral term).

   - Pitch limit kept at 30 deg (Xanthos's standard envelope for

     yo-yo profiles, which routinely use 20-30 deg dive/climb).

     The 20 deg seen in X9827208.obd was a mission-specific override.

   - Filter time constant uo_tau halved (5 s -> 2.5 s).

   - Max heading rate doubled (0.1 -> 0.2 rad/s).

   - Bug fix: heading was 90 RADIANS (~5156 deg). Now 90 deg

     declared with (deg) so the loader converts to radians.

